  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be functions satisfying&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>y</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>y</mi></mfenced><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then which of the following statements is/are TRUE?</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Vasx2",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable at every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tEIjx",
      "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;is differentiable at every<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ljecL",
      "text": "The derivative <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
